      "body": "Finding description and impact\n## Root Cause\n\nThe distributeRewards() function in Distributor.sol contains a critical integer underflow vulnerability in the yield calculation logic. Specifically, at line 386 in the yield calculation loop:\n\n```solidity\nuint256 balance_ = IERC20(yieldToken_).balanceOf(address(this));\nuint256 underlyingYield_ = (balance_ - depositPool.lastUnderlyingBalance).to18(decimals_);\n```\n\nThe code performs subtraction without checking if balance_ is greater than or equal to depositPool.lastUnderlyingBalance. When balance_ < depositPool.lastUnderlyingBalance, Solidity 0.8+ automatically reverts the transaction with panic code 0x11 (arithmetic underflow).\nTrigger Scenarios\n\nThis vulnerability can be triggered by several legitimate DeFi scenarios where token balances decrease:\n\n    * AAVE Slashing Events: aTokens can lose value due to protocol slashing mechanisms\n\n    * Token Fees: Some ERC20 tokens charge fees on transfers or holdings, reducing the contract's balance\n\n    * Deflationary Mechanics: Tokens with burn mechanisms that reduce total supply\n\n    * Liquidation Events: Forced liquidations can reduce held token balances\n\n    * Protocol Upgrades: Administrative functions that affect token balances\n\n    * Precision Loss: Rounding errors in complex DeFi integrations\n\n## Impact Assessment\n\nThe vulnerability has CRITICAL severity with the following impacts:\n\nImmediate Impact:\n\n    Complete denial of service (DOS) for the reward distribution system\n\n    All calls to distributeRewards() will revert with panic(0x11)\n\n    Users cannot receive their earned rewards\n\n    Protocol functionality is completely halted\n\nPersistence:\n\n    The DOS condition persists until manual intervention\n\n    lastUnderlyingBalance never gets updated due to transaction reverts\n\n    Every subsequent call will hit the same underflow condition\n\n    Affects all users, including protocol administrators\n\nFinancial 